# Mobtick PWA — Full-Stack Error & Bug Analysis Report

> **Date:** 2026-03-25 | **Scope:** All backend + frontend source files

---

## 🔴 CRITICAL — Security Vulnerabilities

### 1. Hardcoded Stripe Secret Key in Frontend
**File:** [App.js](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/customer/src/App.js#L21)

```js
const stripePromise = loadStripe("pk_test_51SDlnFJq0C8bwqHF...");
```

The Stripe **publishable key** is hardcoded directly in the source instead of reading from `REACT_APP_STRIPE_KEY` in [.env](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/backend/.env). This makes key rotation impossible without redeploying code.

**Fix:** Replace with `loadStripe(process.env.REACT_APP_STRIPE_KEY)`.

---

### 2. Weak/Placeholder JWT Secret
**File:** [backend/.env](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/backend/.env#L7)

```
JWT_SECRET="mobtick-jwt-secret-change-in-production"
```

This is a guessable, placeholder secret. Anyone who guesses it can forge auth tokens.

**Fix:** Generate a **long random string** (64+ chars) for production.

---

### 3. Placeholder Stripe Webhook Secret
**File:** [backend/.env](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/backend/.env#L6)

```
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET="whsec_your_webhook_secret_here"
```

This is a placeholder — **webhook signature verification will always fail**, meaning the `/webhook` endpoint is effectively broken and anyone can send fake payment events.

---

### 4. OTP Stored in Plain Text
**File:** [routes/auth.js](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/backend/routes/auth.js#L89-L97)

The OTP is stored as plaintext in MongoDB. If the database is compromised, all pending OTPs are exposed.

**Fix:** Hash the OTP with `bcrypt` before storing, and compare hashed values during verification.

---

### 5. Order Creation Has No Authentication
**File:** [routes/order.js](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/backend/routes/order.js#L10)

```js
router.post("/", async (req, res) => { ... });
```

Anyone can create orders without being logged in. No [verifyToken](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/backend/middleware/auth.js#10-26) middleware is applied.

**Fix:** Add [verifyToken](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/backend/middleware/auth.js#10-26) middleware: `router.post("/", verifyToken, async (req, res) => { ... })`.

---

### 6. Payment Intent Creation Has No Authentication
**File:** [routes/payment.js](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/backend/routes/payment.js#L6)

```js
router.post("/create-payment-intent", async (req, res) => { ... });
```

Anyone can create Stripe payment intents without being authenticated. A malicious actor could spam your Stripe account.

---

### 7. Review Submission Has No Authentication
**File:** [routes/reviewRoute.js](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/backend/routes/reviewRoute.js#L30)

Anyone can submit reviews without logging in, enabling spam and fake reviews.

---

### 8. Order Stats & Customer Data Are Publicly Accessible
**File:** [routes/order.js](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/backend/routes/order.js#L61-L223)

`GET /api/order/customers` and `GET /api/order/stats` expose **all customer data** (names, emails, phones, addresses) and business statistics to anyone without authentication.

---

## 🟠 BUGS — Functional Issues

### 9. CORS Wildcard with `credentials: true` Conflict
**File:** [server.js](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/backend/server.js#L18-L24)

```js
cors({
    origin: process.env.FRONTEND_URL || "*",
    credentials: true,
})
```

If `FRONTEND_URL` is not set, `origin: "*"` with `credentials: true` will be **rejected by browsers** (CORS spec forbids this combination). Cookies and auth headers will fail silently.

**Fix:** Always set `FRONTEND_URL` in [.env](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/backend/.env), or use a function to dynamically allow origins.

---

### 10. Fake "LOGOUT" Buttons Don't Actually Log Out
**Files:** [Watches.js:63](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/customer/src/pages/Watches.js#L63), [Cart.js:128](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/customer/src/pages/Cart.js#L128), [Chatbot.js:129](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/customer/src/pages/Chatbot.js#L129)

Multiple pages have a "LOGOUT" button that just navigates to `/home` without clearing tokens from `localStorage`. The real logout logic exists only in [Navbar.js](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/customer/src/Components/Navbar.js).

**Impact:** Users think they logged out but their session persists.

---

### 11. No Route Protection (Authenticated Routes)
**File:** [App.js](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/customer/src/App.js#L48-L78)

All routes (`/cart`, `/buynow`, `/chatbot`, etc.) are accessible without login. There's no `ProtectedRoute` wrapper that checks for `authToken` in `localStorage`.

**Impact:** Unauthenticated users can access the entire app.

---

### 12. Cart Duplicate-Saves to `localStorage`
**File:** [Cart.js](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/customer/src/pages/Cart.js#L27-L52)

The cart is saved to `localStorage` in **three different places**: (1) inside the `location.state` effect, (2) inside [updateQuantity](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/customer/src/pages/Cart.js#63-74), and (3) in a `useEffect` watching `cartItems`. This causes redundant writes and potential race conditions.

**Fix:** Remove the inline `localStorage.setItem` calls from effects at L43 and L70. Keep only the `useEffect` at L50-52.

---

### 13. Express 5 Compatibility Issue — `express.raw()` Middleware
**File:** [server.js](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/backend/server.js#L29)

The project uses **Express 5** (`"express": "^5.1.0"`) but uses `express.raw()` which may behave differently in v5. Express 5 removed several legacy middleware features. This should be tested.

---

### 14. Navbar Has Duplicate `<header>` Elements
**Files:** Multiple pages ([Cart.js](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/customer/src/pages/Cart.js#L103), [BuyNow.js](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/customer/src/pages/BuyNow.js#L288), [Watches.js](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/customer/src/pages/Watches.js#L29), [ProductPage.js](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/customer/src/pages/ProductPage.js#L138), [Chatbot.js](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/customer/src/pages/Chatbot.js#L99))

The [Navbar](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/customer/src/Components/Navbar.js#10-150) component is shown via [Layout](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/customer/src/App.js#23-36) in [App.js](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/customer/src/App.js), but **Cart, BuyNow, Watches, ProductPage, and Chatbot all render their own custom headers** with inconsistent behavior (fake logout, separate dark mode toggle). This creates UI inconsistency and maintenance burden.

---

### 15. `via.placeholder.com` Fallback Images Will Break
**File:** [ProductPage.js:95](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/customer/src/pages/ProductPage.js#L95)

```js
image: p.imageUrl || "https://via.placeholder.com/400x300?text=No+Image"
```

`via.placeholder.com` is unreliable and frequently goes offline. Use a local placeholder image instead.

---

### 16. Seller Model Has Password Hash in Pre-Save Hook (Double Hashing Risk)
**File:** [models/seller.js](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/backend/models/seller.js#L11-L14)

The Seller model has a `pre("save")` hook that hashes the password. But there's **no seller signup route** — only a login route. If a seller is created manually with an already-hashed password and later saved again (e.g., profile update), the hash could be double-hashed.

---

### 17. Dark Mode State Not Persisted
**Files:** Every page (Cart, BuyNow, Watches, ProductPage, Chatbot, Login, Signup)

Each page manages its own `darkMode` state independently with `useState(true)`. Navigating between pages resets the user's preference. 

**Fix:** Use a React Context or `localStorage` to persist dark mode preference across the app.

---

## 🟡 WARNINGS — Code Quality / Architecture

### 18. No Input Validation on Backend Order Fields
**File:** [routes/order.js](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/backend/routes/order.js#L27-L29)

```js
if (!customer?.name || !totalAmount || !paymentMode) {
```

Only `customer.name`, `totalAmount` and `paymentMode` are validated. `totalAmount` is trusted from the client — a malicious user could send `totalAmount: 0` for expensive items.

**Fix:** Calculate `totalAmount` server-side from product prices in the database.

---

### 19. No Rate Limiting
**Files:** All routes

There's no rate limiting on any route (login, signup, payment, etc.). This enables:
- Brute-force password attacks
- OTP flooding (sending unlimited emails)
- API abuse

**Fix:** Add `express-rate-limit` middleware.

---

### 20. `FRONTEND_URL` Not Set in [.env](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/backend/.env)
**File:** [backend/.env](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/backend/.env)

`FRONTEND_URL` is referenced in [server.js](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/backend/server.js) CORS config but is **not defined** in the [.env](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/backend/.env) file, so it falls back to `"*"` (see Bug #9).

---

### 21. Inconsistent Error Response Format
**Files:** Various routes

Some routes return `{ success: false, msg: "..." }`, others return `{ error: "..." }`, and others return `{ message: "..." }`. The frontend must handle all three patterns.

| Route | Error Format |
|-------|-------------|
| [auth.js](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/backend/routes/auth.js) | `{ success, msg }` |
| [order.js](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/backend/models/order.js) | `{ error }` |
| [reviewRoute.js](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/backend/routes/reviewRoute.js) | `{ message }` |
| [payment.js](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/backend/routes/payment.js) | `{ error }` |
| [productRoutes.js](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/backend/routes/productRoutes.js) | `{ success, msg }` |

---

### 22. `WhatsApp Image` File in Backend Directory
**File:** [backend/WhatsApp Image 2025-08-04 at 12.25.04.jpeg](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/backend/WhatsApp%20Image%202025-08-04%20at%2012.25.04.jpeg)

A random WhatsApp image (178KB) is sitting in the backend root directory. This should be removed.

---

### 23. `uploads/` Directory Not Served Statically
**File:** [server.js](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/backend/server.js)

Multer is configured in [auth.js](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/backend/routes/auth.js) to save files to `uploads/`, but [server.js](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/backend/server.js) never calls `app.use("/uploads", express.static("uploads"))`. Uploaded files are not accessible via HTTP.

---

### 24. Payment Route Mounted at `/api` Not `/api/payment`
**File:** [server.js:71](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/backend/server.js#L71)

```js
app.use("/api", paymentRoutes);
```

The payment route handler defines `/create-payment-intent`, so the full path becomes `/api/create-payment-intent` instead of the more RESTful `/api/payment/create-payment-intent`. This is inconsistent with other route mounting patterns.

---

### 25. No Seller Signup Route
**File:** [routes/auth.js](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/backend/routes/auth.js)

There's a seller login route (`POST /api/auth/seller/login`) but **no seller signup** route. Sellers must be manually added to the database.

---

### 26. Product `imageUrl` Validator Rejects Valid URLs
**File:** [models/product.js:57-63](file:///c:/Users/Zainab/OneDrive/Documents/Desktop/ZDesktop/Mobtick%28PWA%29/backend/models/product.js#L57-L63)

```js
return /^https?:\/\/.+\.(jpg|jpeg|png|webp|gif)(\?.*)?$/i.test(url);
```

This regex rejects valid URLs that have path segments after the extension (e.g., `https://cdn.example.com/image.jpg/resize/500x500`). It also rejects URLs with fragments (`#`).

